Data processed by third-party SDKs (as declared in Google Play Data safety)

This section lists, for Queens, the data processed by the third-party SDKs included in the app. It matches the Data safety form of the app on Google Play.

- Google AdMob (advertising): collects and shares with Google the advertising ID / app set ID and other device identifiers, an approximate location derived from your IP address, ad interactions (impressions, clicks) and diagnostics (such as app launches and performance). Purposes: advertising, ad measurement and analytics, and fraud prevention and security. We do not receive your name or contact details from AdMob.
- Firebase Analytics (Google): app interactions (events and screens viewed), the Firebase installation ID / device identifiers, and basic device and app information. Purposes: analytics and app functionality.
- Firebase Crashlytics (Google): crash logs and diagnostics (stack trace, device model, Android and app version, a random installation ID). Purposes: analytics and app stability.
- Firebase Cloud Messaging (Google): a push token / Firebase installation ID, used to deliver notifications. Purpose: app functionality.
- Daily leaderboard (Firebase Authentication and Cloud Firestore, Google): when you finish the daily puzzle, Queens signs you in anonymously (no email, no password, no name) and stores on Google's servers a randomly generated alias (for example "IndigoPanda92"), your solving time, the puzzle size and date, and a random anonymous user ID. It is used to show the top times and your rank. The alias is generated by the app and is not linked to your identity; you cannot type a name or any personal data into it. Data travels encrypted (HTTPS/TLS). Each entry carries a 7-day expiry date; automatic deletion on that date is being enabled, and old entries are removed on request. To ask us to delete your entry, write to tll.developers.apps@gmail.com with your alias. Purpose: app functionality. Data safety types: User IDs and Other in-app activity (collected, not shared, not used for advertising).

Friends league (optional, from version 1.8): the friends league only exists if you tap "Join the league". Joining creates an anonymous Firebase Authentication account (a random user ID, no email, no phone number, no name) and stores on Firebase Cloud Firestore: a nickname and avatar generated by the app (you cannot type free text), your friend code, your friendships and, for each daily puzzle you solve, its result (your solve time, the number of hints used, your streak and the time it was recorded). We do not store your name, email, location, contacts or your board.

Only friends you have accepted can read your results, and only your nickname, avatar and results are visible to them. You can remove or block anyone at any time. The app deletes your own results after about two weeks, and we also purge expired data from the server periodically.

You can delete all your league data (nickname, friendships, results, blocks and the anonymous account) in Settings > Delete my league data. You can also ask us to do it by writing to tll.developers.apps@gmail.com and quoting your friend code. The optional reminder "friends have played" is a notification created on your phone; no notification is sent from a server. If you open an invitation link, the Google Play Install Referrer API gives the app the friend code that was in the link, once, after installing.

The anonymous account is the same one the app already uses for the optional daily leaderboard (a generated alias and your solve time, kept for 7 days). Deleting your league data also deletes that account.

Consent: where required (European Economic Area, United Kingdom, Switzerland) the app asks for your consent through Google's User Messaging Platform (UMP) before showing ads.
Ad choices: you can reset or delete your advertising ID and opt out of ads personalisation in Android Settings > Google > Ads.
Security: data sent to these services travels encrypted in transit (HTTPS/TLS).
Data deletion: the app has no user accounts with personal data (the daily leaderboard and the optional friends league use an anonymous ID and a generated alias; see above). If you joined the friends league, delete your league data in Settings > Delete my league data, or write to tll.developers.apps@gmail.com quoting your friend code. Data stored on your device is deleted by uninstalling the app or clearing its data; for data held by Google (advertising ID, analytics), reset your advertising ID as described above or write to tll.developers.apps@gmail.com and we will help with the request.

